Reviews of the theorem statements against their docstrings, each in two rounds: Gemini (gemini-4-argon through
~/.local/bin/agy-readonly, run in a read-only snapshot of the files at the commit under review) and a fresh Claude
reviewer (a subagent with no context but review-prompt-*.txt, reading the same snapshots).  Round 2's prompt says
what was concluded about round 1.

Round 1 (code of 756100a before the review changes): both found that plan_no_resend covered retries only (a 307/308
follow could in principle resend a streamed body), that nothing tied the target URI to Hop.origin, that rule 7 held
only on the hop where the method changed, that the 429/503 opt-in and followRedirects off had no theorem, and
docstrings that claimed more than their statements.  All fixed (plan_follow_replayable, Reachable.target,
Reachable.emptyBody, plan_retry_status, plan_no_follow, plan_follow_new_hop, rewritten docstrings, Clock.wallSec
without a default).  Kept by design, with reasons in the round-2 prompt: a refused 3xx at the hop limit is
delivered; Host may be absent (the client writes it from the target); Retry-After dates are measured from Date;
307/308 resend a POST as a redirect, not a retry.  Refuted: header-name case (Header.Name is lower case by
construction) and default-port mismatch (URI.port defaults by scheme).  Out of scope: stale docstrings of
Cause.localClose and Cause.isConnect in Error.lean.

Round 2: both found that no theorem kept the body empty on hops after a method change (fixed:
plan_follow_keeps_empty) and that plan_follow_replayable's "delivered instead" was unproved (fixed:
plan_refused_delivered, plan_off_delivered).  Gemini found that a credential field named by the first request's
Connection was given back on a return to the original origin (fixed in start, with a unit test).  The Claude
reviewer noted that a Host the first request gives is kept on same-origin hops (now documented as intended, for
virtual hosts) and that "only http and https" had a test but no theorem (added Reachable.scheme); Gemini that the
causes never retried and the cross-origin Referer rule had no plan-level theorem (added plan_no_retry and
plan_follow_cross_origin).  Not acted on: today's Client.plan refuses https, which the wiring must change.
